  "question": {
    "text": "There are 4 men and 5 women in Group A, and 5 men and 4 women in Group B. If 4 persons are selected from each group, then the number of ways of selecting 4 men and 4 women is _____",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5626",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{|l|l|l|}\n\\hline {\\begin{array}{c} \n\\text{From} \\\\\n\\text{Group A}\n\\end{array}} & {\\begin{array}{c} \n\\text{From} \\\\\n\\text{Group B}\n\\end{array}} & \\text{Ways of selection} \\\\\n\\hline 4 \\mathrm{M} & 4 \\mathrm{~W} & { }^4 \\mathrm{C}_4{ }^4 \\mathrm{C}_4=1 \\\\\n\\hline 3 \\mathrm{M} 1 \\mathrm{~W} & 1 \\mathrm{M} 3 \\mathrm{~W} & { }^4 \\mathrm{C}_3{ }^5 \\mathrm{C}_1{ }^5 \\mathrm{C}_1{ }^4 \\mathrm{C}_3=400 \\\\\n\\hline 2 \\mathrm{M} 2 \\mathrm{~W} & 2 \\mathrm{M} 2 \\mathrm{~W} & { }^4 \\mathrm{C}_2{ }^5 \\mathrm{C}_2{ }^5 \\mathrm{C}_2{ }^4 \\mathrm{C}_2=3600 \\\\\n\\hline 1 \\mathrm{M} 3 \\mathrm{~W} & 3 \\mathrm{M} 1 \\mathrm{~W} & { }^4 \\mathrm{C}_1{ }^5 \\mathrm{C}_3{ }^5 \\mathrm{C}_3{ }^4 \\mathrm{C}_1=1600 \\\\\n\\hline 4 \\mathrm{~W} & 4 \\mathrm{M} & { }^5 \\mathrm{C}_4{ }^5 \\mathrm{C}_4=25 \\\\\n\\hline \\text{ Total } & \\text{5626} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}$",
